# ============================================================================
# REACT-ROUTER (dashboard bundle inside the server image)
# ============================================================================
# Expires: 2026-11-01
#
# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2: "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action Execution Before
# 400 Response". Only exploitable in react-router's RSC (React Server
# Components / framework) mode, where server actions execute during request
# handling. The vonzio dashboard uses react-router-dom in plain LIBRARY mode
# (<BrowserRouter> + <Routes> in packages/dashboard/src/App.tsx, bundled by
# vite as a static SPA) — there is no RSC runtime, no server actions, and no
# react-router code executing on the server at all. The fixed version (8.3.0)
# is a major upgrade; taking it for an unreachable code path isn't worth the
# churn right now.
#
# When this expires: re-evaluate upgrading react-router-dom to v8 (or later)
# as its ecosystem settles, or renew with the same justification if the
# dashboard still doesn't use RSC mode.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# ============================================================================
# TYPESCRIPT NATIVE COMPILER (agent-base image only)
# ============================================================================
# Expires: 2026-11-01
#
# CVE-2026-56852 (golang.org/x/text v0.38.0, norm.Iter infinite loop) and
# CVE-2026-39822 (Go stdlib) are compiled into Microsoft's prebuilt
# @typescript/typescript-linux-x64 native tsc binary — we cannot rebuild it,
# only Microsoft can bump its toolchain. Both are DoS-class (hang/loop), and
# tsc only ever processes workspace source inside the sandboxed agent
# container (unprivileged user, PID + memory limits, no host access). Worst
# case is a wedged compile in a disposable container — not a security
# boundary crossing.
#
# When this expires: `npm view typescript version` and rebuild agent-base —
# a typescript release built with Go x/text >= 0.39.0 clears both. Renew
# with the same justification if Microsoft hasn't shipped one.
CVE-2026-56852
CVE-2026-39822

# ============================================================================
# GO TOOLCHAIN CVEs IN PREBUILT BINARIES (agent-base image only)
# ============================================================================
# Expires: 2026-11-15
#
# Go stdlib / x/net / x/text advisories published in October 2026, found in
# two binaries we install prebuilt and cannot rebuild:
#   - /usr/bin/gh: GitHub CLI 2.102.0 (latest release), built with Go 1.27.1;
#     fixed in Go 1.27.2 and x/net 0.60.0.
#   - Microsoft's native tsc (typescript 7.0.2, latest), built with Go 1.26.4
#     and x/text 0.38.0.
# Every entry is denial-of-service class except CVE-2026-56858 (html/template
# XSS), which needs a binary that renders HTML templates to a browser; neither
# does. gh is an HTTPS client talking to GitHub's API, tsc processes workspace
# source with no network listener, and both run only inside the sandboxed
# agent container (unprivileged user, PID + memory limits, no host access).
# Worst case is a hung command in a disposable container.
#
# When this expires: rebuild agent-base. A gh release built with Go >= 1.27.2
# and a typescript release built with Go >= 1.26.9 / x/text >= 0.41.0 clear
# these; delete the entries Trivy no longer reports and renew the rest.
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56851
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031
